 34AL c  2001Pr08: {+197}Au({+34}Al,{+34}Al'|g). E=68.1 MeV/nucleon radioactive 
 34AL2c  beam of {+34}Al was produced by fragmentation of an 80-MeV/nucleon     
 34AL3c  {+48}Ar primary beam on a 376-mg/cm{+2} {+9}Be primary target,         
 34AL4c  separated by the NSCL A1200 fragment separator, and bombarded on the   
 34AL5c  702 mg/cm{+2} {+197}Au secondary target at 59.70 MeV/nucleon middle of 
 34AL6c  energy. Beams passing through the target were detected and stopped in a
 34AL7c  cylindrical fast-slow plastic phoswich detector located at zero        
 34AL8c  degrees. The |g rays were detected using the NSCL NaI(Tl) array.       
 34AL9c  Measured E|g, I|g, and (scattered-{+34}Al)|g-coin. Deduced |g          
 34ALAc  production cross sections and B(E2). Also see 2000PrZX.                
